Subject: register VM: registers stop owning their values under deferred RC (stage D4)

What this does:
  Stage D4 of the deferred-RC plan
  (`HP-S3-DEFERRED-RC-PLAN-2026-10-02.md` section 3) flips register stores
  to non-owning. With D1 (register windows published as roots), D2 (zero-count
  table + reconcile) and D3 (exact-count fixes, back-edge drain) in place, a
  register write no longer dups the new value or releases the old one; a value
  whose count reaches zero is parked and freed by reconcile only if no live
  register refers to it. Variables, owned argument copies, object slots and
  closure cells stay owning, so every store from a register into one of them
  now takes its own reference.

  Boundaries that had to change:
  - stores out of registers (locals, args via `regvm_put_arg`, object fill,
    return-to-C, catch unwind, for-of wrappers) dup;
  - a suspended coroutine's window owns while parked (`rv_owns_regs`,
    `js_regvm_drc_suspend`/`_resume`), including the initial yield, and
    `async_func_mark`/`async_func_free` only walk it when it owns;
  - a coroutine frame's arg_buf is owned (`async_func_init` dups it) even
    though it is resumed with `argv == arg_buf`, so `arg_owned` includes
    `JS_CALL_FLAG_GENERATOR`;
  - a record call borrows the caller's register window for arguments only
    when the callee cannot write back through a reference
    (`regvm_args_borrowable`: no captured arg, no mapped `arguments`, no
    `make_arg_ref`; new `JSFunctionBytecode.args_captured`, also derived on
    bytecode read);
  - atoms: a dropped atom's string may still sit in a register, so
    `__JS_FreeAtom` parks it with `js_drc_zero`, and `JS_FreeAtomStruct`
    turns a parked atom back into a plain string so the deferred free does not
    remove it from the atom table a second time;
  - `JS_FreeRuntime` sets `drc_in_reconcile` after the final drain so
    teardown frees are immediate.

  Measured (`fixed.js`, i7-8700): 28,965,011,626 -> 24,485,406,348
  instructions (-15.5 %) and 13,701,132,294 -> 11,480,932,913 cycles
  (-16.2 %); peak RSS 13,472 KB. Checksum `546.1008391043414`, diff-suite
  `pass=398 fail=0 skip=0` mono and threaded, leak check clean, ASan+UBSan
  box2d clean, test262 built-ins/language/annexB/staging error sets equal to
  head (head additionally crashes in language/statements; D4 does not).

